import json, pathlib
r=pathlib.Path('.')
ids=[f'SR-STR-{i:03d}' for i in range(7,13)]
batch='SR-BATCH-LITERATURE_SEARCH-02-R01'
task='SR-SEARCH-01'
ledger='docs/structure-radar/literature/SR-SEARCH-02.md'
desired={'SR-STR-007':'ACTIVE','SR-STR-008':'ACTIVE','SR-STR-009':'ACTIVE','SR-STR-010':'ACTIVE','SR-STR-011':'ACTIVE','SR-STR-012':'EXTERNAL_GATE'}
rp=r/'docs/structure-radar/structure-registry.json'; reg=json.loads(rp.read_text()); cards={c['structure_id']:c for c in reg['structures']}
pp=r/'docs/structure-radar/progress.json'; prog=json.loads(pp.read_text())
existing=next((x for x in prog['audit_batches'] if x.get('batch_id')==batch),None)
if existing is None:
    for cid in ids:
        c=cards[cid]
        assert c['search_status']=='NOT_SEARCHED',(cid,c['search_status'])
        assert c['card_status']=='NORMALIZED',(cid,c['card_status'])
        if cid=='SR-STR-012': assert c['arsenal_decision']=='EXTERNAL_GATE',c['arsenal_decision']
        else: assert c['arsenal_decision']=='PENDING',(cid,c['arsenal_decision'])
        c['search_status']='SEARCHED'; c['arsenal_decision']=desired[cid]; c['search_ledger']=ledger
    rp.write_text(json.dumps(reg,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    prog['audit_batches'].append({'batch_id':batch,'task_id':task,'status':'SUBMITTED_FOR_AUDIT','source_ids':[],'sources_reviewed':0,'structures_added':0,'structures_updated':6,'structure_carrier_sources':0,'structures_deduped':0,'searches_completed':6,'arsenal_decisions':5,'audit_required':True,'duplicate_source':0,'no_distinct_structure':0})
    pp.write_text(json.dumps(prog,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    lp=r/ledger; lp.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    lp.write_text('''# StructureRadar literature ledger — search batch 02\n\nSEARCH_TASK=SR-SEARCH-01\nBATCH_ID=SR-BATCH-LITERATURE_SEARCH-02-R01\nSEARCH_DATE=2026-08-19\nSTRUCTURES=SR-STR-007,SR-STR-008,SR-STR-009,SR-STR-010,SR-STR-011,SR-STR-012\nEVIDENCE_POLICY=primary sources for external theorem claims; repo arsenal checked first\nNOVELTY_BY_SEARCH_ABSENCE=false\n\n## SR-STR-007 — Directional exactly-two face-mask identities\nRepo identity: `N2,a=A_ab,ac-A3`, `N2,b=A_ab,bc-A3`, `N2,c=A_ac,bc-A3`; directional contrasts cancel the common `A3` exactly. Existing weapon: `S23-W02`. This is exact inclusion/exclusion on repo incidence masks, not a literature-dependent theorem. Transfer verdict: `REPO_EXACT_IDENTITY; NO_EXTERNAL_UPGRADE_NEEDED`. Smallest transfer test: reproduce the exactly-two truth table and preserve the same directional incidence measure. Arsenal decision: `ACTIVE`.\n\n## SR-STR-008 — Thin but infinite space-diagonal cover of the exactly-two-face host\nRepo theorem: `B^(1/4) << N2(B) <<_epsilon B^(1/2+epsilon)`, hence `N2/M2 -> 0` while `N2 -> infinity`; true exponent unresolved. Existing weapons: `S24-W-THIN-COVER`, `S25-W01`, `S25-W03` and the Stage14 half-power upper interface. Takumi Yoshida, arXiv:2407.09825 (2024), gives a 32:1 surjection from elliptic-curve data to equivalence classes of rational face cuboids and proves infinitude, but not the repo primitive-canonical integer Euclidean-height corridor. Browning--Loughran, arXiv:1705.01999, gives general rational-point sieve/thin-set machinery but not this corridor without exact model/height adapters. Transfer verdict: `ADJACENT_INFINITUDE + GENERAL_THIN_SET_METHOD; NO_STRONGER_DIRECT_HEIGHT_COLLISION`. Arsenal decision: `ACTIVE`.\n\n## SR-STR-009 — Euler-completion proportion on the unmarked at-least-two-face host\nRepo object: `H_ge2=M2+M3`, `Phi=M3/(M2+M3)`, `Phi -> 0`. Existing exact weapon: `S26-W02 Phi`. Primary Euler-brick literature located does not state this same-measure primitive-canonical Euclidean-height completion ratio. General toric Manin/equidistribution results govern the ambient side only after repo-specific model/height identification and do not independently count the Euler-brick numerator under the exact height. Transfer verdict: `REPO_MEASURE_ADAPTER + EXISTING_AUDITED_COUNTING_INPUTS; NO_DIRECT_EXTERNAL_RATIO`. Keep distinct from raw incidence `P=M2+3M3` and adjacent-stratum `M3/M2`. Arsenal decision: `ACTIVE`.\n\n## SR-STR-010 — Multiplicity-three Euler-completion proportion on raw face-pair incidences\nRepo object: `P_j=M2,j+M3`, `P=M2+3M3`, `Theta_j=M3/P_j`, `Theta=3M3/(M2+3M3)`. Existing weapons: `S25-W05` and `S26-W02 Theta`. Factor three is exact incidence multiplicity, not an independence factor. No primary source found states the exact raw-incidence cuboid measure with the repo Euclidean-height corridor. Transfer verdict: `REPO_EXACT_MULTIPLICITY_ADAPTER; NO_DIRECT_EXTERNAL_RAW_INCIDENCE_COLLISION`. Smallest transfer test: each Euler brick contributes three raw face-pair incidences and once to each directional `P_j`. Arsenal decision: `ACTIVE`.\n\n## SR-STR-011 — Balanced Cayley-Gaussian packet normal form\nRepo object: every active Stage14 face is covered by finitely decorated Cayley/Gaussian strips after gcd, sign, 2-primary and dyadic localization. Existing weapon: `AR-007`. Classical Euclid/Gaussian parametrizations explain individual Pythagorean faces, but the balanced strip, common-core bookkeeping, physical masks and Stage14 height ranges are repo-specific. Focused primary-source search found no theorem with this exact packet measure and decorations. Transfer verdict: `CLASSICAL_ALGEBRAIC_CONTEXT + REPO_SPECIFIC_NORMAL_FORM`. Smallest transfer test: preserve gcd, sign, 2-primary, dyadic, cutoff and face/space masks in both directions. Arsenal decision: `ACTIVE`.\n\n## SR-STR-012 — Uniform elliptic finite-fiber degree bridge\nRepo object: `E_t:Y^2=X(X-1)(X+t^2)` plus rational 2-torsion and polynomial model/point height control yields `deg_B(F)=B^o(1)`. Existing interface: `AR-005`. Marta Dujella, arXiv:2312.03655 (2023), Theorem 1.1, gives a uniform `exp(C log B/log log B)` bound for rational points of exponential height at most `B` on elliptic curves over a fixed number field with a rational point of exact prime order, above the curve-height threshold; for `ell=2` this applies over `Q`. Francesco Naccarato, arXiv:2105.04032 (2021), proves the same quality over `Q` with one nontrivial rational 2-torsion point. Repo reuse still needs a uniform polynomial comparison from physical cutoff to theorem point height and curve-height threshold. Transfer verdict: `EXTERNAL_THEOREM_FOUND; EXACT_MODEL_AND_HEIGHT_ADAPTER_REQUIRED`. Smallest transfer test: nonsingularity, rational 2-torsion, fixed-degree Weierstrass change, `h(E_t)=O(log B_phys)`, and point exponential height `<=B_phys^C` uniformly. Arsenal decision: `EXTERNAL_GATE` retained.\n\n## Batch decision\nSEARCHES_COMPLETED=6\nARSENAL_DECISIONS_RESOLVED_FROM_PENDING=5\nEXISTING_ACTIVE_WEAPONS_CONFIRMED=5\nEXTERNAL_GATES_CONFIRMED=1\nNEW_EXTERNAL_ACTIVE_WEAPONS=0\nDIRECT_STRONGER_SAME_POPULATION_HEIGHT_COLLISIONS=0\nNOVELTY_BY_SEARCH_ABSENCE=false\nPERFECT_CUBOID_EXISTENCE_PROMOTED=false\nPERFECT_CUBOID_NONEXISTENCE_PROMOTED=false\n''')
else:
    for cid in ids:
        assert cards[cid]['search_status']=='SEARCHED'
        assert cards[cid]['arsenal_decision']==desired[cid]
        assert cards[cid].get('search_ledger')==ledger
